{"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "query": "Unit tests for an Arduino Uno module: Washing machine safety controller (fill, wash, spin, door interlock, alarms). Pins: pin 2 INPUT door reed switch, LOW = closed (not connected in the test setup: reads LOW); pin 3 INPUT_PULLUP tilt switch to GND, HIGH = shaking (not connected in the test setup: reads HIGH); pin 10 OUTPUT passive buzzer (tone); pin 11 OUTPUT water valve relay; pin 12 OUTPUT red LED, door locked; pin 13 OUTPUT green LED, door open; pin 14 INPUT water level sensor A0 (not connected: reads 0); pin 15 INPUT three buttons on a resistor ladder A1: ~1019 / ~509 / ~338 (not connected: reads 0 = none); pin 4 OUTPUT LCD RS (16x2, pins 4..9 parallel); pin 16 OUTPUT stepper IN1..IN4 on A2..A5 (28BYJ-48). Arduino API used: abs, analogRead, digitalRead, digitalWrite, millis, noTone, pinMode, tone. Libraries: LiquidCrystal. Library API used: begin, clear, display, noDisplay, setCursor. Simulated devices: none. Functions to test: void washer_init(), void washer_loop(), void washer_loop_with(uint32_t now_ms, int btn_adc, bool door_closed, bool tilt_high, int water_adc), int washer_decode_button(int adc), int washer_water_percent(int adc), bool washer_is_running_state(State s), State washer_state(), State washer_paused_from(), bool washer_paused_by_door(), bool washer_paused_by_imbalance(), int washer_active_melody(), bool washer_melody_playing(), bool washer_lcd_on(), const char* washer_lcd_line(uint8_t row).", "embedding": [-0.029754638671875, 0.00939178466796875, -0.03857421875, -0.0245513916015625, -0.020233154296875, 0.01007080078125, -0.00882720947265625, -0.041168212890625, 0.017822265625, 0.0171661376953125, 0.018829345703125, -0.032989501953125, -0.045623779296875, 0.037689208984375, 0.02630615234375, 0.018707275390625, 0.019866943359375, 0.0114288330078125, -0.058746337890625, 0.04949951171875, 0.0670166015625, -0.0038547515869140625, 0.023529052734375, -0.0031833648681640625, -0.00183868408203125, -0.05035400